  "id": "COMPOUND:29952 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Citral is implicated in the interaction with A549 through a series of molecular pathways involving the enzyme MOVP-3, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound, in turn, shows a target relationship with A549, as observed across multiple paths. The evidence suggests that Citral may act as a modulator of the downstream pathway, influencing the activity of MOVP-3 and thereby affecting A549. The consistent presence of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a common target across different cell lines indicates a potential role in the regulation of A549, though the exact mechanism of Citral's involvement remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Citral in modulating the expression or function of the downstream target, which could be relevant in understanding its biological effects.",
